   "date": "2020-06-25T16:15:40Z",
   "subject": "Plot individual heterozygosity and missing data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">Hi,</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">I am quite new to DartR and bioinformatics in general.</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">Therefore, thank you for such a </span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">comprehensive guide to this extremely useful package and for this very helpful group.</span></font></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">I would like to check if there is a correlation between individual heterozygosity and missing data, particularly at a specific</span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\">minimum coverage (5), to see if I should</span></font><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><font color=\"#000000\"> increase this threshold slightly.</font></span></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:12px\"><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></span></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Is there an easy way to plot this?</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Thank you in advance.</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Best,</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Ana</span></font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tsy6_ncZBgAJ",
   "from": "Arthur Georges",
   "author": "a3ea45e87285d820",
   "date": "2020-06-26T00:55:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: Plot individual heterozygosity and missing data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Anna,</div><div><br></div><div>Try this.</div><div><br></div><div># Grab the test set<br>  gl &lt;- <a href=\"http://testset.gl\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://testset.gl&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792459128765000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Upm3dxOD9AQWrBNbIMRXv\">testset.gl</a><br># Assign each individual as a population<br>  pop(gl) &lt;- indNames(gl)<br># Calculate Heterozygosity<br>  hetro &lt;- gl.report.heterozygosity(gl)<br># Display heterozygosity<br>  hetro$Ho    <br># Calculate the call rate by individual<br>  ind.call.rate &lt;- 1 - rowSums(<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792459128765000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3vF6u53g46Fxw3Aw7Ra0bI\">is.na</a>(as.matrix(gl)))/nLoc(gl)<br># Display call rate<br>  ind.call.rate<br>#Plot heterozygosity against call rate<br>  plot(x=ind.call.rate,y=hetro$Ho)</div><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
